<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tower of skulls</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as towers of skulls</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A tower of skulls was a structure built from the heads of the slain, raised as a deliberate display of terror after the capture of a city. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> was notorious for constructing such towers during his campaigns. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a> profile describes them as a calculated psychological weapon that convinced many cities to surrender without resistance, reducing military costs while maximising terror.</p></div>
